# API Conventions

- All API routes are mounted under `/api`
- Use RESTful resource naming: `/products`, `/cart`, `/orders`
- Use standard HTTP methods: GET, POST, DELETE
- Request/response bodies are JSON
- Authentication via `x-user` header (user ID)
- Error responses: `{ "error": "message" }` with appropriate status codes
  - 400: validation error, business rule violation
  - 401: missing/invalid authentication
  - 404: resource not found
  - 500: internal server error
- Successful responses return the resource directly (not wrapped)
- List endpoints return arrays
- IDs are strings (e.g., `p1`, `ord_12345_abcdef`)
- Money values are numbers (USD, no cents integer)
- Dates are ISO 8601 strings in JSON